$$------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ Rubber single-element uniaxial tension  --  Altair OptiStruct
$$
$$   units : mm - N - tonne - s   (stress MPa, density 1.10-9)
$$   model : 1 x 1 x 1 mm CHEXA, 1/8 symmetry, x-face pulled to u = 1.0 mm
$$           (stretch lambda = 2, i.e. 100% engineering strain)
$$   check : sigma_x ~= 4.7162 MPa, reaction on the pulled face ~= 2.3606 N
$$
$           The closed-form INCOMPRESSIBLE answer is 4.7250 MPa; these decks
$           set K/G = 1000, and that 0.1% of volume change lowers it to 4.7162.
$           J = 1.001048 at the end, so the section is 0.500524 mm2, not 0.5.
$$   TWO OptiStruct-specific points, both from Altair's own nonlinear FEA book:
$$     1. "MATHE materials are referenced by PLSOLID property, which is a
$$        property dedicated exclusively for nonlinear hyperelastic materials."
$$        So this deck uses PLSOLID, NOT PSOLID.
$$     2. "Since it is a large displacement analysis, LGDISP card should be
$$        activated (together with HASHASSM,YES)."
$$
$$   material : generalized Mooney-Rivlin, C10 = 0.6, C01 = 0.15 MPa,
$$              K = 1500 MPa (K/G = 1000 with G0 = 2(C10+C01) = 1.5 MPa)
$$
$$   run   : optistruct rubber-1elem-optistruct.fem
$$------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ I/O Options
SCREEN,OUT
OUTPUT,H3D
DISPLACEMENT(H3D) = ALL
STRESS(H3D)       = ALL
STRAIN(H3D)       = ALL
SPCFORCE(H3D)     = ALL
$$
$$ Subcase Information
SUBCASE 1
  LABEL    = stretch to lambda = 2
  ANALYSIS = NLSTAT
  SPC      = 1
  LOAD     = 2
  NLPARM   = 10
$$
BEGIN BULK
$
PARAM,LGDISP,1
PARAM,HASHASSM,YES
$
$       ID      NINC    DT      KMETHOD KSTEP   MAXITER CONV
NLPARM  10      50              AUTO    5       25      UPW
$
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ MESH
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRID    1               0.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    2               1.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    3               1.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    4               0.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    5               0.0     0.0     1.0
GRID    6               1.0     0.0     1.0
GRID    7               1.0     1.0     1.0
GRID    8               0.0     1.0     1.0
$
CHEXA   1       1       1       2       3       4       5       6
+       7       8
$
$ hyperelastic solids use PLSOLID, not PSOLID
$       PID     MID
PLSOLID 1       1
$
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ MATERIAL
$$   MATHE line 1 : MID, Model, (blank), K, RHO, TEXP, TREF, GE
$$   MATHE line 2 : C10, C01, D1, TAB1, TAB2, TAB3, TAB4, TABD
$$   line 3       : C20, C11, C02, D2, NA, ND
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$       MID     MODEL           K       RHO
MATHE   1       MOONEY          1500.   1.10-9
$       C10     C01     D1
+       0.6     0.15
+                               NA      ND
+                               1       1
$
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ BOUNDARY CONDITIONS   (1/8 symmetry + enforced displacement)
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPC1    1       1       1       4       5       8
SPC1    1       2       1       2       5       6
SPC1    1       3       1       2       3       4
SPC1    1       1       2       3       6       7
$
SPCD    2       2       1       1.0     3       1       1.0
SPCD    2       6       1       1.0     7       1       1.0
$
ENDDATA
